# ML-KEM-768 KAT — FIPS 203
# Format: NIST .rsp style, deterministic. Regenerating yields a byte-identical file
#         (no timestamp unless --stamp).
# Derivation:
#   seed = SHA3-256(BE32(count) || BE32(0x6B65796E) || BE32(0x4D4C4B45))   (d)
#   z    = SHA3-256(seed || "MLKE-z")
#   m    = SHA3-256(BE32(count) || BE32(0x656E6361) || BE32(0x4D4C4B45))
# Fields:
#   seed: 32-byte KeyGen d
#   z:    32-byte KeyGen z
#   m:    32-byte Encaps message
#   ek:   1184-byte encapsulation key
#   dk:   2400-byte decapsulation key = dkPKE || ek || H(ek) || z  (FIPS 203 §7.1)
#   c:    1088-byte ciphertext
#   k:    32-byte shared secret = SHA3-512(m || H(ek))[0:32]
# Verified at generation time (every vector, else the file is not written):
#   V1 decapsulate(dk, c) == k  (this repository's implementation)
#   V2 @noble/post-quantum: keygen(d||z).ek == ek  and  decapsulate(c, dk) == k
#   V3 k == SHA3-512(m || SHA3-256(ek))[0:32]
#   V4 dk layout canonical: dk[1152..2336] == ek, dk[2336..2368] == H(ek), dk[2368..2400] == z
# Re-check: node scripts/ci-mlkem-kat.cjs  |  node scripts/interop/run.mjs run --kat all --partners noble

